        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          This publication examines the effects of spaceflight on the hormonal
responses (bioassayable growth hormone or BGH) to a unilateral plantar flexor exercise protocol. Four male astronauts on STS-78 (LMS) were examined.  Data included are as follows:
<LI>Isometric plantar flexion exercise protocol
<LI>Plantar flexor torque and electromyographic activity of the soleus and medial gastrocnemius muscles during maximal voluntary contractions
<LI>Bioassayable and immunoassayable growth hormone (IGH and BGH)plasma concentrations before and after the exercise test
<LI>Immunoassayable IGF-I plasma concentrations preexercise and postexercise
<LI>Magnitudes of IGH and BGH exercise induced changes before, during, and after spaceflight
<P>
Source: McCall GE, Goulet C, Roy RR, Grindeland RE, Boorman GI, Bigbee AJ, Hodgson JA, Greenisen MC, Edgerton VR. Spaceflight suppresses exercise-induced release of bioassayable growth hormone. J Appl Physiol 1999 Sep; 87(3):1207-12.
        </div>

